#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""Uniparental disomy (UPD) segments of a family's members, from its norm.bcf.

Two subcommands, one for each place the upd step runs them.

family
    Reads `bcftools query -f '%CHROM\\t%POS\\t%INFO/UPD_AF[\\t%GT\\t%GQ\\t%DP]\\n'` of the family's
    biallelic SNVs on stdin (UPD_AF is the gnomAD frequency the task annotated), its sample
    order from --samples, the family's inputs snapshot (written by the pipeline: its pedigree
    rows, normalised, with which members are in the BCF and which have a coverage JSON), the
    coverage JSONs, and the roh step's roh.tsv and froh.tsv when there are, and writes
    <prefix>.segments.tsv, <prefix>.events.tsv and <prefix>.members.tsv.

cohort
    From every family's three tables, writes the cohort's: the family tables concatenated, and
    on the events, how many other families have an overlapping event (recurrent).

Members and modes. Every member in the BCF is analysed, in the best mode its family allows. A
parent counts only when it is in the BCF: a parent written 0, a DUMMY_ parent or one without a
gVCF is missing.
    trio  both parents in the BCF: a hidden Markov model of the child's genotypes given its
          parents', with UPDhmm's five states, N (one allele from each parent), iso_mat and
          iso_pat (both alleles copies of one homolog of that parent), het_mat and het_pat (both
          homologs of that parent: the child's genotype is the parent's), and three more states
          of normal inheritance, where the parents share a haplotype:
            auto     the two haplotypes the child got are one: the autozygosity of consanguinity
                     and of chance ROH. Its genotypes are those of an isodisomy, but where the
                     other parent lacks the child's allele
            ibd_mat  the father's haplotype the child got is the mother's other one: the child's
                     genotype is the mother's, as in het_mat, but where the parents are opposite
                     homozygotes
            ibd_pat  the same, the other way round
          So an isodisomy or a heterodisomy is called on the Mendelian errors it explains, not
          on a ROH or a run of genotypes identical to a parent's, which short haplotypes shared
          by unrelated parents give all over the genome. No allele frequency is needed.
    duo   one parent P in the BCF: the same five states, the missing parent Q transmitting the
          ALT with its gnomAD frequency p. iso_Q (both alleles one draw at p) and het_Q (two
          draws at p) rest on opposite homozygotes with P, which normal inheritance never gives.
          iso_P is also what autozygosity looks like, and het_P what related parents can, so
          they are only trusted when the rest of the genome is outbred (the isolation rule,
          below), and held to the extents of solo mode.
    solo  no parent in the BCF, founders included: isodisomy only, from the roh step's ROH
          segments (bcftools roh with ancestry-matched frequencies). Heterodisomy cannot be seen
          without a parent. The roh step's segments at most SOLO_ROH_JOIN_MB of covered genome
          apart are one ROH (the roh step splits a ROH at the panel's gaps, and a stray genotype
          splits one too); the ROH of ISOLATION_ROH_MB or more are the runs. A run at
          DELETION_DEPTH_MAX of the depth or less is a deletion,
          a lost copy reading as a ROH (a 15q11-q13 deletion as one of 4.8 Mb), and is set aside.
          The other runs are candidates when the rest of the genome is outbred:
            whole_chromosome  a run spans WHOLE_CHROMOSOME_SPAN of the chromosome
            multiple          two runs or more of SOLO_TERMINAL_MB on one chromosome, made one
                              event: the isodisomic parts of a mixed UPD, whose crossovers leave
                              heterodisomy between them, more often than chance
            terminal          a run reaching an end of the chromosome, SOLO_TERMINAL_MB long
            interstitial      a run of SOLO_INTERSTITIAL_MB
          Terminal ROH rarely occurs without UPD, while an interstitial one needs 15-20 Mb to
          stand out from chance and consanguinity (ACMG, del Gaudio et al. 2020). On a chromosome
          with an imprinted region, any of them marks a possible UPD of the whole chromosome,
          whose heterodisomic parts a ROH cannot show: a maternal UPD15 is mostly heterodisomy.
          The ROH need not reach the imprinted region (ACMG), so the imprinting the event carries
          is that of every imprinted region of the chromosome, and an interstitial event there is
          medium, not low. The roh step's
          upd_candidate_chrom, the chromosome holding most of the long ROH, is noted, not taken
          for a whole-chromosome isodisomy: one long interstitial ROH makes it.
A trio or duo in which a parent fails the parentage rule (below) is redone without that parent.

Sites. A genotype counts at GQ >= 20 and DP >= 10, with alleles 0 and 1 only, and DP at most
MAX_DP_FACTOR times the member's median (collapsed repeats). A position with more than one
record, a multiallelic site split by bcftools norm, is dropped: -m2 -M2 does not remove them.
With --mask, the roh step's panel sites (its bundle's roh/sites.tsv.gz), a site outside the
panel's covered segments is dropped: runs of panel sites at most MASK_MAX_GAP apart, from the
first to the last. The panel leaves out centromeres, heterochromatin, the MHC, the acrocentric
arms and segmental duplications, where Mendelian errors cluster from mismapped reads and read as
short UPDs (most of the false calls of two real families). A chromosome the panel does not hold
(chrX) is not masked. A
site enters a member's model when the members it uses are all called there and one of them
carries the ALT; the likelihoods are conditioned on that, so the sites the BCF holds only
because a relative is variant do not bias them. Autosomes, and chrX outside the PARs for a
member with two X: karyotype XX from its coverage JSON, or with none, a female pedigree sex and
an X heterozygosity of at least X_HET_TWO_X_MIN. On X the father is hemizygous (a heterozygous
call of his counts as missing) and het_pat cannot occur.

Emissions. A parent of genotype g transmits the ALT with probability g/2. Each state gives the
child's genotype a distribution; an observed genotype is the true one with probability
1 - GENOTYPE_ERROR, and either other one otherwise. The gnomAD frequency is clamped to
[AF_MIN, AF_MAX], so that no single site can dominate, and a site absent from gnomAD gets AF_MIN.

Segments. Viterbi per chromosome. Entering or leaving a UPD state, or changing its parent, costs
SWITCH per site; going between the iso and het states of one parent, as a mixed UPD does at its
crossovers, costs MIX_SWITCH; going between N and the shared-haplotype states costs
AUTO_SWITCH. A segment is a run of one UPD state, cut wherever two of its sites are more than
SEGMENT_MAX_GAP apart: a segment never spans a region with no site, such as one the mask removed,
so its length is covered genome. With LR the likelihood of a
site under the segment's state over N:
    lod              sum of log10 LR over the segment's sites: the score
    n_informative    sites where LR is at least 2-fold either way
    n_supporting     sites favouring the state at least 2-fold
    n_contradicting  sites favouring N at least 2-fold, such as a child het inside an isodisomy
    n_strong         sites favouring the state at least 10-fold, which N explains only as an
                     error: in a trio the Mendelian errors the state explains, in a duo the
                     opposite homozygotes with the present parent. A UPD of the present parent
                     in a duo has few: its evidence is many sites each about 2-fold (a child
                     identical to its parent where the parent is heterozygous)
    support_fraction n_supporting / (n_supporting + n_contradicting)
    depth_ratio      the child's mean DP over the segment's sites, over its mean DP genome-wide
A solo segment is scored at the child's non-reference SNVs inside it: a hom-alt site has
probability 1 - SOLO_HET_IN_ROH in a ROH and p / (2 - p) otherwise, a het site SOLO_HET_IN_ROH
and 2(1 - p) / (2 - p).

Interpretation. A depth ratio at or below DELETION_DEPTH_MAX is a deletion: the child has one
copy, which looks like an isodisomy of the other parent. It is set aside, never an event: this
step calls UPD, and leaves CNVs to the CNV callers (WisecondorX). Segments of one member, chromosome and
parent of origin at medium confidence or more, and at most EVENT_GAP_MB of covered genome apart
(a gap with no site does not count, so the two arms of a chromosome join across its centromere),
make one event:
iso, het or mixed; whole_chromosome when it spans at least WHOLE_CHROMOSOME_SPAN of the
chromosome's sites, segmental otherwise; terminal when it reaches either end. A low segment
makes no event, and only the segments of events are written. An event spanning one of the
IMPRINTED regions (GRCh38 windows around the GENCODE spans of their imprinted genes) carries the
disorder its parent of origin implies there; a trio or duo event outside them carries none, a
terminal UPD of distal 15q, say, not Prader-Willi, since a trio sees the heterodisomic parts
too. A solo event carries those of every imprinted region of its chromosome (above).

Siblings. Two children sharing a parent in the BCF, with events on one chromosome overlapping by
SIBLING_OVERLAP of the shorter, share an artefact, a parental CNV or reads mismapped alike, not a
UPD: a UPD is sporadic. Both events are then low, whatever their origin, unless the two are MZ
twins (genotypes discordant at MZ_MAX_DISCORDANCE or less of the sites they are called at), who
share their UPDs.

Confidence of a segment, and of an event (its best segment's):
    high    lod >= HIGH_LOD, at least HIGH_MIN_MB long, depth ratio within DEPTH_NORMAL, and
            n_strong >= HIGH_STRONG; for a UPD of the present parent in a duo, whose evidence is
            weak site by site, n_supporting >= HIGH_SUPPORT instead
    medium  lod >= MEDIUM_LOD, at least MEDIUM_MIN_MB long, and n_strong >= MEDIUM_STRONG (or
            n_supporting >= MEDIUM_SUPPORT)
    low     the rest
    Both high and medium also need a support fraction of MIN_SUPPORT_FRACTION. A trio state, a
    duo's present-parent state, and an isodisomy of its missing parent (the child homozygous)
    predict the child's genotypes closely, so a real UPD is all but never contradicted (1.00 on
    the real events seen, the known UPD15 as either duo included), where a mapping artefact is
    (0.11-0.85). A heterodisomy of a duo's missing parent draws both of the child's alleles
    from the population, so a share of its sites favour N by chance (0.69 in simulation): it
    needs MIN_DIFFUSE_HET_SUPPORT.
    solo: whole_chromosome high, multiple and terminal medium, interstitial low (medium on a
    chromosome with an imprinted region), any of them low with a depth outside DEPTH_NORMAL.
An iso_P or het_P event of a duo is held to the extents of solo mode: high only over a whole
chromosome, medium for a terminal one, low for an interstitial one, and not written below
those; and it is low when the member is not isolated. Short haplotypes shared by the parents
make a child identical to the parent it has, which a duo cannot tell from a UPD: they gave
dozens of short events per duo child.

Isolation. The member's F_ROH at segments of at least ISOLATION_ROH_MB on the other autosomes,
over their span, is below ISOLATION_MAX_FROH, and its parents, when the roh step measured them,
are not related beyond the 4th degree (kinship <= PARENTS_KINSHIP_MAX). The roh step's segments
are used when there are; a duo without them uses its own iso_P segments. These are the roh
step's constants for upd_candidate_chrom.

Parentage. A child and a parent are opposite homozygotes (0/0 against 1/1) at more than
PARENTAGE_MAX_OPPOSITE of the autosomal sites where both are called and one carries the ALT,
outside the child's UPD segments: about 0.1% for a parent and its child, 8% for unrelated people
(sampleqc's PO_OPPOSITE_HOM_MAX). It is not that parent's child, or not the sample it is named
after, which sampleqc's NOT_PARENT reports. That parent is dropped and the child redone.

Cohort. An event is recurrent when events of RECURRENT_MIN_FAMILIES other families or more
overlap it on the same chromosome, each by at least RECURRENT_OVERLAP of both: a region where the
calls are artefacts more often than UPD.
"""

import argparse
import bisect
import glob
import gzip
import json
import math
import os
import sys
from array import array

MIN_GQ = 20
MIN_DP = 10
MAX_DP_FACTOR = 2.5
MASK_MAX_GAP = 300000
SEGMENT_MAX_GAP = 300000
AF_MIN = 0.001
AF_MAX = 0.999
AF_BINS = 1000
GENOTYPE_ERROR = 0.002
SWITCH = 1e-8
MIX_SWITCH = 1e-4
AUTO_SWITCH = 1e-4
EVENT_GAP_MB = 5.0
SOLO_HET_IN_ROH = 0.02
SOLO_TERMINAL_MB = 5.0
SOLO_INTERSTITIAL_MB = 15.0
SOLO_ROH_JOIN_MB = 1.0
TERMINAL_SLACK_MB = 2.0
ISOLATION_ROH_MB = 1.5
ISOLATION_MAX_FROH = 0.01
PARENTS_KINSHIP_MAX = 0.0221
DELETION_DEPTH_MAX = 0.75
DEPTH_NORMAL = (0.8, 1.25)
WHOLE_CHROMOSOME_SPAN = 0.9
HIGH_LOD = 20.0
HIGH_STRONG = 20
HIGH_SUPPORT = 50
HIGH_MIN_MB = 2.0
MEDIUM_LOD = 10.0
MEDIUM_STRONG = 10
MEDIUM_SUPPORT = 20
MEDIUM_MIN_MB = 0.5
MIN_SUPPORT_FRACTION = 0.9
MIN_DIFFUSE_HET_SUPPORT = 0.5
SIBLING_OVERLAP = 0.5
MZ_MAX_DISCORDANCE = 0.02
PARENTAGE_MAX_OPPOSITE = 0.01
X_HET_TWO_X_MIN = 0.1
SEX_TOLERANCE = 0.25
RECURRENT_MIN_FAMILIES = 3
RECURRENT_OVERLAP = 0.5
# GRCh38 pseudoautosomal regions, 1-based inclusive
PARS = ((10001, 2781479), (155701383, 156030895))

AUTOSOMES = [str(i) for i in range(1, 23)]
STATES = ["N", "iso_mat", "het_mat", "iso_pat", "het_pat", "auto", "ibd_mat", "ibd_pat"]
UPD_STATES = (1, 2, 3, 4)
SHARED_STATES = (5, 6, 7)
DUO_STATES = 5
ORIGIN = {"iso_mat": "maternal", "het_mat": "maternal", "iso_pat": "paternal", "het_pat": "paternal"}
SIBLING = {1: 2, 2: 1, 3: 4, 4: 3}
MISSING = 3
LN10 = math.log(10)

# Imprinted regions, GRCh38, 1-based: windows around the GENCODE spans of their imprinted genes
# (from the gene BED of the lab's references): PLAGL1 143.94 Mb; GRB10 50.59-50.73, PEG10/SGCE
# 94.59-94.66, MEST 130.49-130.51; IGF2 2.13, KCNQ1 2.44-2.85, CDKN1C 2.88 (H19 lies just distal
# of IGF2); DLK1 100.73 to RTL1 100.88 (MEG3 between them); MKRN3 23.57 to UBE3A 25.41; GNAS
# 58.84-58.91. The disorders by parent of origin, after del Gaudio et al. 2020 and Scuffins et al.
IMPRINTED = {
    "6": [(143900000, 144000000, "6q24", {"paternal": "transient neonatal diabetes"})],
    "7": [(50550000, 50750000, "7p12", {"maternal": "Silver-Russell"}),
          (94550000, 94700000, "7q21", {"maternal": "Silver-Russell"}),
          (130450000, 130550000, "7q32", {"maternal": "Silver-Russell"})],
    "11": [(1900000, 2900000, "11p15.5", {"maternal": "Silver-Russell", "paternal": "Beckwith-Wiedemann"})],
    "14": [(100700000, 100900000, "14q32", {"maternal": "Temple", "paternal": "Kagami-Ogata"})],
    "15": [(23500000, 25500000, "15q11-q13", {"maternal": "Prader-Willi", "paternal": "Angelman"})],
    "20": [(58800000, 58950000, "20q13", {"maternal": "Mulchandani-Bhoj-Conlin",
                                          "paternal": "pseudohypoparathyroidism 1B"})],
}

SEGMENT_COLUMNS = ["family_id", "sample", "mode", "father", "mother", "chrom", "start", "end", "length_mb",
                   "state", "origin", "source", "n_sites", "n_informative", "n_supporting", "n_contradicting",
                   "n_strong", "support_fraction", "lod", "depth_ratio", "roh_fraction", "interpretation",
                   "confidence", "event_id"]
EVENT_COLUMNS = ["family_id", "sample", "mode", "event_id", "chrom", "start", "end", "length_mb", "origin",
                 "composition", "extent", "terminal", "n_segments", "n_supporting", "n_strong",
                 "support_fraction", "lod", "depth_ratio", "interpretation", "imprinting", "confidence",
                 "shared_with", "notes"]
LOG2 = math.log10(2)
MEMBER_COLUMNS = ["family_id", "sample", "father", "mother", "mode", "father_used", "mother_used", "chrx",
                  "n_sites", "error_rate", "status", "n_events", "n_events_high"]


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def die(msg):
    print(f"ERROR: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)


def fmt(value, digits=4):
    if value is None:
        return "."
    if isinstance(value, bool):
        return "yes" if value else "no"
    if isinstance(value, float):
        if math.isnan(value) or math.isinf(value):
            return "."
        return f"{value:.{digits}f}"
    return str(value)


def as_float(text):
    try:
        value = float(text)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    return None if math.isnan(value) else value


def write_tsv(path, columns, rows):
    with open(path, "w") as fh:
        fh.write("\t".join(columns) + "\n")
        for row in rows:
            fh.write("\t".join(fmt(row.get(c)) for c in columns) + "\n")


def read_tsv(path):
    with open(path) as fh:
        header = fh.readline().rstrip("\n").lstrip("#").split("\t")
        rows = []
        for line in fh:
            line = line.rstrip("\n")
            if line:
                rows.append(dict(zip(header, line.split("\t"))))
    return header, rows


def chrom_name(chrom):
    return chrom[3:] if chrom.startswith("chr") else chrom


def in_par(pos):
    return any(a <= pos <= b for a, b in PARS)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Snapshot
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_snapshot(path):
    """Members in pedigree order: sample -> dict(fid, father, mother, sex, sequenced, coverage).
    Header lines start with '#'; parents are '0' when unknown, sex 1, 2 or 0."""
    members = {}
    with open(path) as fh:
        for line in fh:
            line = line.rstrip("\n")
            if not line or line.startswith("#"):
                continue
            cols = line.split("\t")
            if len(cols) != 7:
                die(f"{path}: snapshot row with {len(cols)} columns instead of 7: {line}")
            fid, sample, father, mother, sex, sequenced, coverage = cols
            members[sample] = {"fid": fid, "father": father, "mother": mother,
                               "sex": {"1": "male", "2": "female"}.get(sex, "unknown"),
                               "sequenced": sequenced == "yes", "coverage": coverage}
    if not members:
        die(f"{path} has no member")
    return members


def read_coverage(directory, sample, tag):
    if not directory or tag in ("-", ""):
        return None
    path = os.path.join(directory, f"{sample}.{tag}.json")
    if not os.path.exists(path):
        die(f"{sample} has coverage {tag} in the snapshot, and no {path}")
    with open(path) as fh:
        return json.load(fh)


def karyotype(coverage):
    """cnv_coverage's coverage sex, from its chrX and chrY ratios; None without them."""
    if coverage is None or coverage.get("chrX_ratio") is None or coverage.get("chrY_ratio") is None:
        return None
    x, y = 2 * coverage["chrX_ratio"], 2 * coverage["chrY_ratio"]
    nx, ny = int(round(x)), int(round(y))
    if abs(x - nx) > SEX_TOLERANCE or abs(y - ny) > SEX_TOLERANCE or nx == 0:
        return "ambiguous"
    return "X0" if (nx, ny) == (1, 0) else "X" * nx + "Y" * ny


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sites
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Chrom:
    """The sites of one chromosome: positions, gnomAD frequency bins, and per sample a dosage
    (0, 1, 2 or MISSING) and a depth."""

    def __init__(self, name, n_samples):
        self.name = name
        self.pos = array("l")
        self.af = array("H")
        self.g = [bytearray() for _ in range(n_samples)]
        self.dp = [array("H") for _ in range(n_samples)]

    def __len__(self):
        return len(self.pos)


def af_bin(text):
    p = as_float(text)
    if p is None:
        p = AF_MIN
    p = min(max(p, AF_MIN), AF_MAX)
    return int(round(p * AF_BINS))


def parse_genotype(gt, gq, dp):
    """(dosage, depth); dosage MISSING unless both alleles are 0 or 1 at GQ and DP high enough."""
    depth = as_float(dp)
    depth = 0 if depth is None else min(int(depth), 65535)
    quality = as_float(gq)
    if quality is None or quality < MIN_GQ or depth < MIN_DP or len(gt) != 3 or gt[1] not in "/|":
        return MISSING, depth
    a, b = gt[0], gt[2]
    if a not in "01" or b not in "01":
        return MISSING, depth
    return (a == "1") + (b == "1"), depth


def read_mask(path):
    """chromosome -> sorted (starts, ends) of the panel's covered segments: runs of its sites at
    most MASK_MAX_GAP apart."""
    covered = {}
    with gzip.open(path, "rt") as fh:
        header = fh.readline().rstrip("\n").split("\t")
        if header[:2] != ["chrom", "pos"]:
            die(f"{path} does not start with the columns chrom, pos")
        last = {}
        for line in fh:
            chrom, pos = line.split("\t", 2)[:2]
            chrom, pos = chrom_name(chrom), int(pos)
            starts, ends = covered.setdefault(chrom, (array("l"), array("l")))
            if chrom in last and pos - last[chrom] <= MASK_MAX_GAP:
                ends[-1] = pos
            else:
                starts.append(pos)
                ends.append(pos)
            last[chrom] = pos
    return covered


def masked(mask, chrom, pos):
    """Whether a site falls outside the mask's covered segments, on a chromosome it holds."""
    if mask is None or chrom not in mask:
        return False
    starts, ends = mask[chrom]
    i = bisect.bisect_right(starts, pos) - 1
    return i < 0 or pos > ends[i]


def read_sites(stream, n_samples, mask=None):
    """chromosome name -> Chrom, for chr1-22 and X. Every record of a position held more than
    once is dropped, and with a mask every site outside it."""
    chroms = {}
    wanted = set(AUTOSOMES) | {"X"}
    previous, duplicated = None, False

    def keep(record):
        name, pos, af, genotypes = record
        chrom = chroms.get(name)
        if chrom is None:
            chrom = chroms[name] = Chrom(name, n_samples)
        chrom.pos.append(pos)
        chrom.af.append(af)
        for i, (d, depth) in enumerate(genotypes):
            chrom.g[i].append(d)
            chrom.dp[i].append(depth)

    expected = 3 + 3 * n_samples
    for line in stream:
        fields = line.rstrip("\n").rstrip("\t").split("\t")
        if len(fields) != expected:
            die(f"a bcftools query line has {len(fields)} fields, not 3 and 3 for each of {n_samples} samples")
        name = chrom_name(fields[0])
        if name not in wanted:
            continue
        pos = int(fields[1])
        if masked(mask, name, pos):
            continue
        if previous is not None and previous[0] == name and previous[1] == pos:
            duplicated = True
            continue
        if previous is not None and not duplicated:
            keep(previous)
        genotypes = [parse_genotype(fields[3 + 3 * i], fields[4 + 3 * i], fields[5 + 3 * i])
                     for i in range(n_samples)]
        previous, duplicated = (name, pos, af_bin(fields[2]), genotypes), False
    if previous is not None and not duplicated:
        keep(previous)
    return chroms


def median_depths(chroms, n_samples):
    """Each sample's median depth over its called autosomal sites, from a histogram."""
    medians = []
    for i in range(n_samples):
        hist = {}
        for name in AUTOSOMES:
            chrom = chroms.get(name)
            if chrom is None:
                continue
            g, dp = chrom.g[i], chrom.dp[i]
            for j in range(len(chrom)):
                if g[j] != MISSING:
                    hist[dp[j]] = hist.get(dp[j], 0) + 1
        total = sum(hist.values())
        median, seen = None, 0
        for depth in sorted(hist):
            seen += hist[depth]
            if 2 * seen >= total:
                median = depth
                break
        medians.append(median)
    return medians


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Emissions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def observe(true):
    """Observed genotype distribution from the true one, with the genotyping error."""
    return [(1 - GENOTYPE_ERROR) * t + GENOTYPE_ERROR * (1 - t) / 2 for t in true]


def child_given(transmit_a, transmit_b):
    """Distribution of the child's dosage from two independent transmitted alleles."""
    return [(1 - transmit_a) * (1 - transmit_b),
            transmit_a * (1 - transmit_b) + (1 - transmit_a) * transmit_b,
            transmit_a * transmit_b]


def iso(transmit):
    return [1 - transmit, 0.0, transmit]


def exact(g):
    return [1.0 if c == g else 0.0 for c in range(3)]


def shared_other(g, transmit_other):
    """The haplotype the child got from one parent is the other parent's untransmitted one: the
    child's genotype is the other parent's g, the first parent carrying that haplotype's allele."""
    if (g == 0 and transmit_other == 1) or (g == 2 and transmit_other == 0):
        return [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
    return exact(g)


def autozygous(transmit_a, transmit_b):
    """Two copies of a haplotype both parents carry: its allele is one both can transmit."""
    ref, alt = (1 - transmit_a) * (1 - transmit_b), transmit_a * transmit_b
    if ref + alt == 0:
        return [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
    return [ref / (ref + alt), 0.0, alt / (ref + alt)]


def conditioned(dist, c, condition):
    """log P(child = c), conditioned on the child carrying the ALT when the parents in the model
    do not (the site is only in the model then)."""
    p = dist[c]
    if condition:
        p = p / (1 - dist[0])
    return math.log(p) if p > 0 else float("-inf")


def trio_table(on_x):
    """code (9 father + 3 mother + child) -> log emission per state, the eight of STATES; None when
    the site is not used."""
    table = [None] * 27
    for f in range(3):
        for m in range(3):
            for c in range(3):
                if f == m == c == 0:
                    continue
                if on_x and f == 1:
                    continue
                tf, tm = f / 2, m / 2
                dists = [child_given(tf, tm), iso(tm), exact(m), iso(tf), exact(f), autozygous(tf, tm),
                         shared_other(m, tf), shared_other(f, tm)]
                row = []
                for k, dist in enumerate(dists):
                    # The father has one X: no two homologs of his, and none he did not transmit
                    if on_x and STATES[k] in ("het_pat", "ibd_pat"):
                        row.append(float("-inf"))
                        continue
                    row.append(conditioned(observe(dist), c, f == 0 and m == 0))
                table[9 * f + 3 * m + c] = tuple(row)
    return table


def duo_table(parent_is_father, on_x):
    """code (af bin, 3 parent + child) -> log emission per state, the first five of STATES: none
    of the shared-haplotype states, which a duo cannot tell from iso_P and het_P."""
    table = [None] * ((AF_BINS + 1) * 9)
    for b in range(1, AF_BINS):
        p = b / AF_BINS
        for g in range(3):
            if on_x and parent_is_father and g == 1:
                continue
            t = g / 2
            # P: the present parent, Q: the missing one
            n, iso_p, het_p, iso_q, het_q = child_given(t, p), iso(t), exact(g), iso(p), child_given(p, p)
            present, missing = (iso_p, het_p), (iso_q, het_q)
            mat, pat = (missing, present) if parent_is_father else (present, missing)
            dists = [n, mat[0], mat[1], pat[0], pat[1]]
            for c in range(3):
                if g == c == 0:
                    continue
                row = []
                for k, dist in enumerate(dists):
                    if on_x and STATES[k] == "het_pat":
                        row.append(float("-inf"))
                        continue
                    row.append(conditioned(observe(dist), c, g == 0))
                table[9 * b + 3 * g + c] = tuple(row)
    return table


def solo_table():
    """(af bin, child dosage) -> log10 LR of ROH over Hardy-Weinberg, at a non-reference site."""
    table = {}
    for b in range(1, AF_BINS):
        p = b / AF_BINS
        table[(b, 2)] = math.log10((1 - SOLO_HET_IN_ROH) * (2 - p) / p)
        table[(b, 1)] = math.log10(SOLO_HET_IN_ROH * (2 - p) / (2 * (1 - p)))
    return table


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HMM
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def transitions(k):
    """Log transition matrix of the first k states of STATES."""
    t = [[math.log(SWITCH)] * k for _ in range(k)]
    for j in UPD_STATES:
        t[j][SIBLING[j]] = math.log(MIX_SWITCH)
    normal = [0] + [s for s in SHARED_STATES if s < k]
    for a in normal:
        for b in normal:
            if a != b:
                t[a][b] = math.log(AUTO_SWITCH)
    for j in range(k):
        t[j][j] = math.log(1 - sum(math.exp(x) for i, x in enumerate(t[j]) if i != j))
    return t


TRANSITIONS = {k: transitions(k) for k in (DUO_STATES, len(STATES))}


def viterbi(codes, table):
    """The most likely state at each site. Every transition is at least SWITCH, so a state's best
    predecessor is the best state overall at SWITCH, or one of the few its transitions favour."""
    n = len(codes)
    if n == 0:
        return []
    k = len(table[codes[0]])
    t = TRANSITIONS[k]
    floor = math.log(SWITCH)
    favoured = [[(j, t[j][s]) for j in range(k) if t[j][s] > floor] for s in range(k)]
    start = [floor] * k
    start[0] = 0.0
    for s in SHARED_STATES:
        if s < k:
            start[s] = math.log(AUTO_SWITCH)
    e = table[codes[0]]
    v = [start[s] + e[s] for s in range(k)]
    back = bytearray(n * k)
    states = range(k)
    for i in range(1, n):
        e = table[codes[i]]
        top, top_arg = v[0], 0
        for j in states:
            if v[j] > top:
                top, top_arg = v[j], j
        top += floor
        nv = [0.0] * k
        base = i * k
        for s in states:
            best, arg = top, top_arg
            for j, x in favoured[s]:
                x += v[j]
                if x > best:
                    best, arg = x, j
            nv[s] = best + e[s]
            back[base + s] = arg
        v = nv
    s = max(range(k), key=lambda j: v[j])
    path = bytearray(n)
    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):
        path[i] = s
        s = back[i * k + s]
    return path


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# family
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Member:
    def __init__(self, sample, index, info):
        self.sample, self.index, self.info = sample, index, info
        self.father, self.mother = None, None
        self.mode, self.status, self.chrx = "solo", "analysed", "no"
        self.n_sites, self.errors = 0, 0
        self.segments = []


def depth_mean(chroms, i, cap):
    total, n = 0, 0
    for name in AUTOSOMES:
        chrom = chroms.get(name)
        if chrom is None:
            continue
        g, dp = chrom.g[i], chrom.dp[i]
        for j in range(len(chrom)):
            if g[j] != MISSING and dp[j] <= cap:
                total += dp[j]
                n += 1
    return total / n if n else None


def x_het_rate(chrom, i):
    if chrom is None:
        return None
    het = hom = 0
    for j in range(len(chrom)):
        if in_par(chrom.pos[j]):
            continue
        d = chrom.g[i][j]
        het += d == 1
        hom += d == 2
    return het / (het + hom) if het + hom else None


def model_sites(chrom, member, used, caps):
    """Indices and codes of the sites a member's model uses on a chromosome."""
    child, cc = member.index, caps[member.index]
    gc, dc = chrom.g[child], chrom.dp[child]
    on_x = chrom.name == "X"
    idx, codes = array("l"), array("H")
    if len(used) == 2:
        (fi, fc), (mi, mc) = used
        gf, df, gm, dm = chrom.g[fi], chrom.dp[fi], chrom.g[mi], chrom.dp[mi]
        for j in range(len(chrom)):
            c, f, m = gc[j], gf[j], gm[j]
            if c == MISSING or f == MISSING or m == MISSING or dc[j] > cc or df[j] > fc or dm[j] > mc:
                continue
            if c + f + m == 0 or (on_x and (f == 1 or in_par(chrom.pos[j]))):
                continue
            idx.append(j)
            codes.append(9 * f + 3 * m + c)
    else:
        ((pi, pc),) = used
        gp, dpp, af = chrom.g[pi], chrom.dp[pi], chrom.af
        father_present = member.father is not None
        for j in range(len(chrom)):
            c, g = gc[j], gp[j]
            if c == MISSING or g == MISSING or dc[j] > cc or dpp[j] > pc or c + g == 0:
                continue
            if on_x and ((father_present and g == 1) or in_par(chrom.pos[j])):
                continue
            idx.append(j)
            codes.append(9 * af[j] + 3 * g + c)
    return idx, codes


def runs(path, idx, pos):
    """(state, first, last) of each run of a UPD state in a Viterbi path, cut where two of its
    sites are more than SEGMENT_MAX_GAP apart."""
    out, i, n = [], 0, len(path)
    while i < n:
        s = path[i]
        j = i
        while j + 1 < n and path[j + 1] == s and pos[idx[j + 1]] - pos[idx[j]] <= SEGMENT_MAX_GAP:
            j += 1
        if s in UPD_STATES:
            out.append((s, i, j))
        i = j + 1
    return out


def score_run(chrom, member, idx, codes, table, state, a, b, mean_depth):
    lod = 0.0
    informative = supporting = contradicting = strong = 0
    depth_total = 0
    dp = chrom.dp[member.index]
    for i in range(a, b + 1):
        row = table[codes[i]]
        lr = (row[state] - row[0]) / LN10
        lod += lr
        if lr >= LOG2:
            supporting += 1
            strong += lr >= 1
        elif lr <= -LOG2:
            contradicting += 1
        depth_total += dp[idx[i]]
    informative = supporting + contradicting
    n = b - a + 1
    name = STATES[state]
    start, end = chrom.pos[idx[a]], chrom.pos[idx[b]]
    # A UPD of the parent a duo has: its evidence is many sites, each weak. One of the parent it
    # lacks: the child's alleles drawn from the population, so its support fraction says little
    weak = member.mode == "duo" and (ORIGIN[name] == "paternal") == (member.father is not None)
    diffuse = member.mode == "duo" and not weak
    return {"weak": weak, "diffuse": diffuse, "chrom": chrom.name, "start": start, "end": end, "length_mb": (end - start + 1) / 1e6,
            "state": name.split("_")[0], "origin": ORIGIN[name], "source": "hmm", "n_sites": n,
            "n_informative": informative, "n_supporting": supporting, "n_contradicting": contradicting,
            "n_strong": strong,
            "support_fraction": supporting / (supporting + contradicting) if supporting + contradicting else None,
            "lod": lod, "depth_ratio": (depth_total / n) / mean_depth if mean_depth else None}


def hmm_member(chroms, member, used, caps, mean_depth, tables):
    """Viterbi segments of one member, over the chromosomes its model covers."""
    member.segments, member.n_sites, member.errors = [], 0, 0
    names = AUTOSOMES + (["X"] if member.chrx == "yes" else [])
    for name in names:
        chrom = chroms.get(name)
        if chrom is None:
            continue
        table = tables(name == "X")
        idx, codes = model_sites(chrom, member, used, caps)
        path = viterbi(codes, table)
        member.n_sites += len(codes)
        for s, a, b in runs(path, idx, chrom.pos):
            member.segments.append(score_run(chrom, member, idx, codes, table, s, a, b, mean_depth))
        # Sites the normal state cannot explain, outside the segments: the genotyping error
        for i, code in enumerate(codes):
            if path[i] == 0 and table[code][0] < math.log(10 * GENOTYPE_ERROR):
                member.errors += 1


def classify(segment):
    """(interpretation, confidence) of an HMM segment. A deletion is graded on its evidence as a
    UPD is, its depth keeping it below high."""
    kind = "isodisomy" if segment["state"] == "iso" else "heterodisomy"
    if segment["depth_ratio"] is not None and segment["depth_ratio"] <= DELETION_DEPTH_MAX:
        kind = "deletion"
    lod, length = segment["lod"], segment["length_mb"]
    depth_ok = segment["depth_ratio"] is None or DEPTH_NORMAL[0] <= segment["depth_ratio"] <= DEPTH_NORMAL[1]
    if segment["weak"]:
        high, medium = segment["n_supporting"] >= HIGH_SUPPORT, segment["n_supporting"] >= MEDIUM_SUPPORT
    else:
        high, medium = segment["n_strong"] >= HIGH_STRONG, segment["n_strong"] >= MEDIUM_STRONG
    needed = MIN_DIFFUSE_HET_SUPPORT if segment["diffuse"] and segment["state"] == "het" else MIN_SUPPORT_FRACTION
    supported = segment["support_fraction"] is not None and segment["support_fraction"] >= needed
    high, medium = high and supported, medium and supported
    if lod >= HIGH_LOD and length >= HIGH_MIN_MB and depth_ok and high:
        return kind, "high"
    if lod >= MEDIUM_LOD and length >= MEDIUM_MIN_MB and medium:
        return kind, "medium"
    return kind, "low"


RANK = {"low": 0, "medium": 1, "high": 2}


def chrom_spans(chroms):
    return {name: (c.pos[0], c.pos[-1]) for name, c in chroms.items() if len(c)}


def rest_froh(segments, chrom, spans):
    """F_ROH at segments of ISOLATION_ROH_MB or more on the autosomes other than chrom."""
    span = sum(e - s + 1 for n, (s, e) in spans.items() if n in AUTOSOMES and n != chrom)
    if not span:
        return None
    roh = sum(e - s + 1 for n, s, e in segments if n != chrom and n in AUTOSOMES and
              (e - s + 1) >= ISOLATION_ROH_MB * 1e6)
    return roh / span


def read_roh(roh_path, froh_path):
    """sample -> (segments [(chrom, start, end, n_sites, quality)], froh row)."""
    if not roh_path or not froh_path:
        return None
    segs = {}
    for row in read_tsv(roh_path)[1]:
        segs.setdefault(row["IID"], []).append(
            (chrom_name(row["chrom"]), int(row["start"]), int(row["end"]), row.get("n_sites"), row.get("quality")))
    froh = {row["IID"]: row for row in read_tsv(froh_path)[1]}
    return {s: (segs.get(s, []), froh[s]) for s in froh}


def overlap(a0, a1, b0, b1):
    return max(0, min(a1, b1) - max(a0, b0) + 1)


def roh_fraction(segment, roh_segments):
    if roh_segments is None:
        return None
    length = segment["end"] - segment["start"] + 1
    covered = sum(overlap(segment["start"], segment["end"], s, e) for n, s, e, _, _ in roh_segments
                  if n == segment["chrom"])
    return covered / length


def solo_member(chroms, member, roh, spans, mean_depth, cap, solo):
    """Candidate isodisomies of a member with no parent in the BCF: runs of its ROH segments,
    graded by their extent."""
    member.segments = []
    segs, froh = roh
    simple = [(n, s, e) for n, s, e, _, _ in segs]
    candidate_chrom = chrom_name(froh.get("upd_candidate_chrom", "."))
    kinship = as_float(froh.get("parents_kinship"))
    if kinship is not None and kinship > PARENTS_KINSHIP_MAX:
        member.status = "not_isolated: parents' kinship {}".format(fmt(kinship))
        return
    slack = TERMINAL_SLACK_MB * 1e6
    by_chrom = {}
    for name, start, end, _, quality in segs:
        if name in AUTOSOMES and name in spans:
            by_chrom.setdefault(name, []).append((start, end, quality))
    for name in sorted(by_chrom, key=AUTOSOMES.index):
        rows = sorted(by_chrom[name])
        joined, run = [], [rows[0]]
        for r in rows[1:]:
            if covered_between(chroms.get(name), max(c[1] for c in run), r[0]) <= SOLO_ROH_JOIN_MB * 1e6:
                run.append(r)
            else:
                joined.append(run)
                run = [r]
        joined.append(run)
        runs_of_roh = [run for run in joined if max(c[1] for c in run) - run[0][0] + 1 >= ISOLATION_ROH_MB * 1e6]
        if not runs_of_roh:
            continue
        first, last = spans[name]
        rest = rest_froh(simple, name, spans)
        scored = []
        for run in runs_of_roh:
            segments = [dict(solo_segment(chroms[name], member, s, e, mean_depth, cap, solo), roh_quality=q)
                        for s, e, q in run]
            sites = sum(x["n_sites"] for x in segments)
            depth = sum(x["depth_ratio"] * x["n_sites"] for x in segments if x["depth_ratio"] is not None)
            scored.append({"start": run[0][0], "end": max(c[1] for c in run), "segments": segments,
                           "depth": depth / sites if sites else None})
        # A deletion reads as a ROH: set aside, a CNV for the CNV callers
        others = [r for r in scored if not (r["depth"] is not None and r["depth"] <= DELETION_DEPTH_MAX)]
        candidates = []
        if others and rest is not None and rest < ISOLATION_MAX_FROH:
            whole = [r for r in others if r["end"] - r["start"] + 1 >= WHOLE_CHROMOSOME_SPAN * (last - first + 1)]
            long_runs = [r for r in others if r["end"] - r["start"] + 1 >= SOLO_TERMINAL_MB * 1e6]
            if whole:
                candidates += [("whole_chromosome", r["segments"]) for r in whole]
            elif len(long_runs) >= 2:
                candidates.append(("multiple", [s for r in others for s in r["segments"]]))
            else:
                for r in others:
                    length_mb = (r["end"] - r["start"] + 1) / 1e6
                    if (r["start"] <= first + slack or r["end"] >= last - slack) and length_mb >= SOLO_TERMINAL_MB:
                        candidates.append(("terminal", r["segments"]))
                    elif length_mb >= SOLO_INTERSTITIAL_MB:
                        candidates.append(("interstitial", r["segments"]))
        for k, (kind, segments) in enumerate(candidates):
            for segment in segments:
                segment.update(extent=kind, chain=f"{name}:{k}", rest_froh=rest, candidate=name == candidate_chrom)
                member.segments.append(segment)


def solo_segment(chrom, member, start, end, mean_depth, cap, solo):
    """The score of a ROH segment at the member's non-reference SNVs inside it."""
    name, length_mb = chrom.name, (end - start + 1) / 1e6
    g, dp, af = chrom.g[member.index], chrom.dp[member.index], chrom.af
    lod, supporting, contradicting, strong, depth_total, n = 0.0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
    for j in range(bisect.bisect_left(chrom.pos, start), bisect.bisect_right(chrom.pos, end)):
        d = g[j]
        if d == MISSING or d == 0 or dp[j] > cap:
            continue
        lr = solo[(af[j], d)]
        lod += lr
        if lr >= LOG2:
            supporting += 1
            strong += lr >= 1
        elif lr <= -LOG2:
            contradicting += 1
        depth_total += dp[j]
        n += 1
    return {"chrom": name, "start": start, "end": end, "length_mb": length_mb, "state": "iso",
            "origin": "unknown", "source": "roh", "n_sites": n, "n_informative": supporting + contradicting,
            "n_supporting": supporting, "n_contradicting": contradicting, "n_strong": strong,
            "support_fraction": supporting / (supporting + contradicting) if supporting + contradicting
            else None, "lod": lod,
            "depth_ratio": (depth_total / n) / mean_depth if n and mean_depth else None,
            "roh_fraction": 1.0}


def solo_confidence(segment):
    depth_ok = segment["depth_ratio"] is None or DEPTH_NORMAL[0] <= segment["depth_ratio"] <= DEPTH_NORMAL[1]
    level = {"whole_chromosome": "high", "multiple": "medium", "terminal": "medium", "interstitial": "low"}[segment["extent"]]
    if level == "low" and segment["chrom"] in IMPRINTED:
        level = "medium"
    return "isodisomy", level if depth_ok else "low"


def opposite_rate(chroms, child, parent, caps, segments):
    """Opposite homozygotes of a child and a parent over the autosomal sites both are called at
    and one of them carries the ALT, outside the child's segments."""
    skip = {}
    for s in segments:
        skip.setdefault(s["chrom"], []).append((s["start"], s["end"]))
    n = opposite = 0
    for name in AUTOSOMES:
        chrom = chroms.get(name)
        if chrom is None:
            continue
        gc, dc, gp, dpp = chrom.g[child], chrom.dp[child], chrom.g[parent], chrom.dp[parent]
        spans = skip.get(name, [])
        for j in range(len(chrom)):
            c, g = gc[j], gp[j]
            if c == MISSING or g == MISSING or c + g == 0 or dc[j] > caps[child] or dpp[j] > caps[parent]:
                continue
            if spans and any(a <= chrom.pos[j] <= b for a, b in spans):
                continue
            n += 1
            opposite += abs(c - g) == 2
    return opposite / n if n else None


def parentage_failures(chroms, member, index, caps):
    """(parent role, its opposite homozygote rate) of the first parent the child is not the
    child of, or None."""
    for role in ("father", "mother"):
        parent = getattr(member, role)
        if parent is None:
            continue
        rate = opposite_rate(chroms, member.index, index[parent], caps, member.segments)
        if rate is not None and rate > PARENTAGE_MAX_OPPOSITE:
            return role, rate
    return None


def covered_between(chrom, a, b):
    """The genome between positions a and b that has sites: the stretches between consecutive
    sites at most SEGMENT_MAX_GAP apart."""
    if chrom is None:
        return b - a
    pos = chrom.pos
    total, previous = 0, a
    for k in range(bisect.bisect_right(pos, a), bisect.bisect_left(pos, b)):
        if pos[k] - previous <= SEGMENT_MAX_GAP:
            total += pos[k] - previous
        previous = pos[k]
    if b - previous <= SEGMENT_MAX_GAP:
        total += b - previous
    return total


def event_groups(member, chroms):
    """(chrom, origin, segments) of each event of a member: its segments of one chromosome and
    origin, at most EVENT_GAP_MB of covered genome apart. An HMM segment below medium makes no
    event; every solo segment is a candidate already."""
    groups = {}
    for s in member.segments:
        if s["source"] == "hmm" and (RANK[s["confidence"]] < RANK["medium"] or s["interpretation"] == "deletion"):
            continue
        groups.setdefault((s["chrom"], s["origin"], s.get("chain") or ""), []).append(s)
    order = {n: i for i, n in enumerate(AUTOSOMES + ["X"])}
    out = []
    for (chrom, origin, run), segs in sorted(groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (order[kv[0][0]], kv[0][1], kv[0][2])):
        segs.sort(key=lambda s: s["start"])
        if run:
            # A solo run of ROH, made by solo_member already
            out.append((chrom, origin, segs))
            continue
        chain = [segs[0]]
        for s in segs[1:]:
            if covered_between(chroms.get(chrom), max(c["end"] for c in chain), s["start"]) <= EVENT_GAP_MB * 1e6:
                chain.append(s)
            else:
                out.append((chrom, origin, chain))
                chain = [s]
        out.append((chrom, origin, chain))
    return out


def imprinting_of(chrom, start, end, origin):
    """The disorders the imprinted regions an event spans imply, by its parent of origin. A solo
    event, whose heterodisomic parts are unseen, gets every imprinted region of its chromosome."""
    out = []
    for a, b, region, disorders in IMPRINTED.get(chrom, []):
        spans = not (start > b or end < a)
        if origin == "unknown":
            out.append("{} ({}{})".format(" or ".join(f"{d} if {o}" for o, d in sorted(disorders.items())), region,
                                         "" if spans else ", if the UPD reaches it"))
        elif spans and origin in disorders:
            out.append(f"{disorders[origin]} ({region})")
    return "; ".join(out) or None


def collapse(fid, member, spans, isolation, chroms):
    """Events of one member, from event_groups."""
    events = []
    for s in member.segments:
        s["event_id"] = None
    for chrom, origin, segs in event_groups(member, chroms):
        event_id = f"{member.sample}:{chrom}:{origin}:{segs[0]['start']}"
        for s in segs:
            s["event_id"] = event_id
        start, end = segs[0]["start"], max(s["end"] for s in segs)
        first, last = spans[chrom]
        slack = TERMINAL_SLACK_MB * 1e6
        states = {s["state"] for s in segs}
        sites = sum(s["n_sites"] for s in segs)
        depth = sum(s["depth_ratio"] * s["n_sites"] for s in segs if s["depth_ratio"] is not None)
        confidence = max((s["confidence"] for s in segs), key=RANK.get)
        notes = []
        if member.mode == "solo":
            kind = segs[0]["extent"]
            extent = "whole_chromosome" if kind == "whole_chromosome" else "segmental"
            notes.append("from ROH ({}); rest F_ROH {}".format({
                "multiple": "several runs on the chromosome: the isodisomic parts of a mixed UPD, or chance",
            }.get(kind, kind), fmt(segs[0]["rest_froh"])))
            if segs[0]["candidate"]:
                notes.append("the roh step's upd_candidate_chrom")
        else:
            extent = "whole_chromosome" if (end - start + 1) >= WHOLE_CHROMOSOME_SPAN * (last - first + 1) \
                else "segmental"
            present = member.father if origin == "paternal" else member.mother
            if member.mode == "duo" and present is not None:
                terminal = start <= first + slack or end >= last - slack
                length_mb = (end - start + 1) / 1e6
                cap = "high" if extent == "whole_chromosome" else \
                    "medium" if terminal and length_mb >= SOLO_TERMINAL_MB else \
                    "low" if length_mb >= SOLO_INTERSTITIAL_MB else None
                if cap is None:
                    # Below the solo extents: a haplotype the parents share, most likely
                    for s in segs:
                        s["event_id"] = None
                    continue
                rest = isolation(chrom)
                if rest is None or rest >= ISOLATION_MAX_FROH:
                    confidence = "low"
                    notes.append("UPD of the parent in the duo, not isolated (rest F_ROH {}): "
                                 "autozygosity or related parents look the same".format(fmt(rest)))
                elif RANK[cap] < RANK[confidence]:
                    confidence = cap
                    notes.append("UPD of the parent in the duo: a ROH, or a haplotype the parents share, "
                                 "looks the same; held to the solo extents ({})".format(
                                     "whole chromosome" if extent == "whole_chromosome" else
                                     "terminal" if terminal else "interstitial"))
        interpretation = "UPD"
        imprinting = imprinting_of(chrom, start, end, origin)
        supporting = sum(s["n_supporting"] for s in segs)
        contradicting = sum(s["n_contradicting"] for s in segs)
        events.append({
            "family_id": fid, "sample": member.sample, "mode": member.mode, "event_id": event_id,
            "chrom": chrom, "start": start, "end": end, "length_mb": (end - start + 1) / 1e6, "origin": origin,
            "composition": "mixed" if len(states) > 1 else states.pop(), "extent": extent,
            "terminal": start <= first + slack or end >= last - slack, "n_segments": len(segs),
            "n_supporting": supporting, "n_strong": sum(s["n_strong"] for s in segs),
            "support_fraction": supporting / (supporting + contradicting) if supporting + contradicting else None,
            "lod": sum(s["lod"] for s in segs),
            "depth_ratio": depth / sites if sites else None, "interpretation": interpretation,
            "imprinting": imprinting, "confidence": confidence, "shared_with": None,
            "notes": notes})
    return events


def discordance(chroms, a, b, caps):
    """Share of the autosomal sites two members are called at, one of them carrying the ALT,
    where their genotypes differ: about 0.4 for siblings, the genotyping error for MZ twins."""
    n = differ = 0
    for name in AUTOSOMES:
        chrom = chroms.get(name)
        if chrom is None:
            continue
        ga, da, gb, db = chrom.g[a], chrom.dp[a], chrom.g[b], chrom.dp[b]
        for j in range(len(chrom)):
            x, y = ga[j], gb[j]
            if x == MISSING or y == MISSING or x + y == 0 or da[j] > caps[a] or db[j] > caps[b]:
                continue
            n += 1
            differ += x != y
    return differ / n if n else None


def sibling_artefacts(analysed, members, chroms, index, caps):
    """Mark the events children sharing a parent have in common: an artefact unless they are MZ
    twins. analysed: sample -> its events."""
    children = [s for s in analysed if any(members[s][p] != "0" for p in ("father", "mother"))]
    for i, a in enumerate(children):
        for b in children[i + 1:]:
            if not any(members[a][p] == members[b][p] != "0" for p in ("father", "mother")):
                continue
            shared = []
            for ea in analysed[a]:
                for eb in analysed[b]:
                    if ea["chrom"] != eb["chrom"]:
                        continue
                    ov = overlap(ea["start"], ea["end"], eb["start"], eb["end"])
                    if ov >= SIBLING_OVERLAP * min(ea["end"] - ea["start"] + 1, eb["end"] - eb["start"] + 1):
                        shared.append((ea, eb))
            if not shared:
                continue
            d = discordance(chroms, index[a], index[b], caps)
            mz = d is not None and d <= MZ_MAX_DISCORDANCE
            for ea, eb in shared:
                for e, other in ((ea, b), (eb, a)):
                    e["shared_with"] = ",".join(filter(None, [e["shared_with"], other]))
                    if mz:
                        e["notes"].append(f"also in {other}, an MZ twin (discordance {fmt(d)})")
                    else:
                        e["notes"].append(f"also in the sibling {other}: an artefact, a parental CNV or "
                                          "reads mismapped alike, not a UPD")
                        e["confidence"] = "low"


def cmd_family(args):
    members = read_snapshot(args.snapshot)
    fids = {m["fid"] for m in members.values()}
    if len(fids) != 1:
        die(f"{args.snapshot} holds the families {', '.join(sorted(fids))}, not one")
    fid = fids.pop()
    order = [s for s in args.samples.split(",") if s]
    index = {s: i for i, s in enumerate(order)}
    for s in order:
        if s not in members:
            die(f"the BCF has the sample {s}, which is not a member of {fid} in the snapshot")
    roh = read_roh(args.roh, args.froh)

    chroms = read_sites(sys.stdin, len(order), read_mask(args.mask) if args.mask else None)
    spans = chrom_spans(chroms)
    medians = median_depths(chroms, len(order))
    caps = [MAX_DP_FACTOR * m if m else 65535 for m in medians]
    trio_tables = {False: trio_table(False), True: trio_table(True)}
    duo_tables = {}
    solo = solo_table()

    rows_members, rows_segments, rows_events, analysed = [], [], [], {}
    for sample, info in members.items():
        if not info["sequenced"]:
            continue
        member = Member(sample, index.get(sample), info)
        row = {"family_id": fid, "sample": sample, "father": info["father"], "mother": info["mother"]}
        if member.index is None:
            member.status = "not_in_bcf"
            rows_members.append(dict(row, mode=".", status=member.status, n_events=0, n_events_high=0))
            continue
        i = member.index
        mean_depth = depth_mean(chroms, i, caps[i])
        if mean_depth is None:
            member.status = "no_sites"
            rows_members.append(dict(row, mode=".", status=member.status, n_events=0, n_events_high=0))
            continue

        k = karyotype(read_coverage(args.coverage_dir, sample, info["coverage"]))
        if k is not None:
            member.chrx = "yes" if k == "XX" else "no"
        else:
            rate = x_het_rate(chroms.get("X"), i)
            member.chrx = "yes" if info["sex"] == "female" and rate is not None and rate >= X_HET_TWO_X_MIN \
                else "no"

        member.father = info["father"] if info["father"] in index else None
        member.mother = info["mother"] if info["mother"] in index else None
        excluded = []
        roh_member = roh.get(sample) if roh is not None else None
        while member.father is not None or member.mother is not None:
            used = [(index[p], caps[index[p]]) for p in (member.father, member.mother) if p is not None]
            if len(used) == 2:
                member.mode = "trio"
                hmm_member(chroms, member, used, caps, mean_depth, lambda x: trio_tables[x])
            else:
                member.mode = "duo"
                key = member.father is not None

                def tables(x, key=key):
                    if (key, x) not in duo_tables:
                        duo_tables[(key, x)] = duo_table(key, x)
                    return duo_tables[(key, x)]
                hmm_member(chroms, member, used, caps, mean_depth, tables)
            for s in member.segments:
                s["interpretation"], s["confidence"] = classify(s)
                s["roh_fraction"] = roh_fraction(s, roh_member[0] if roh_member else None)
            failed = parentage_failures(chroms, member, index, caps)
            if failed is None:
                break
            role, rate = failed
            excluded.append("{} {} (opposite homozygotes {})".format(role, getattr(member, role), fmt(rate)))
            setattr(member, role, None)
            member.segments = []
        if excluded:
            member.status = "parentage: " + ", ".join(excluded) + " excluded"

        if member.father is None and member.mother is None:
            member.mode = "solo"
            if roh_member is None:
                member.status = (member.status + "; " if member.status != "analysed" else "") + \
                    ("no_roh_tables" if roh is None else "not_in_roh_tables")
            else:
                solo_member(chroms, member, roh_member, spans, mean_depth, caps[i], solo)
                for s in member.segments:
                    s["interpretation"], s["confidence"] = solo_confidence(s)

        def isolation(chrom, member=member, roh_member=roh_member):
            if roh_member is not None:
                kinship = as_float(roh_member[1].get("parents_kinship"))
                if kinship is not None and kinship > PARENTS_KINSHIP_MAX:
                    return None
                return rest_froh([(n, s, e) for n, s, e, _, _ in roh_member[0]], chrom, spans)
            present = "paternal" if member.father is not None else "maternal"
            own = [(s["chrom"], s["start"], s["end"]) for s in member.segments
                   if s["state"] == "iso" and s["origin"] == present]
            return rest_froh(own, chrom, spans)

        events = collapse(fid, member, spans, isolation, chroms)
        analysed[sample] = events
        for s in member.segments:
            if s["event_id"] is None:
                continue
            rows_segments.append(dict(s, family_id=fid, sample=sample, mode=member.mode,
                                      father=member.father, mother=member.mother))
        rows_events += events
        rows_members.append(dict(row, mode=member.mode, father_used=member.father or ".",
                                 mother_used=member.mother or ".", chrx=member.chrx,
                                 n_sites=member.n_sites if member.mode != "solo" else None,
                                 error_rate=member.errors / member.n_sites if member.n_sites else None,
                                 status=member.status))

    sibling_artefacts(analysed, members, chroms, index, caps)
    for e in rows_events:
        e["notes"] = "; ".join(e["notes"]) or None
    for row in rows_members:
        if row["sample"] in analysed:
            events = analysed[row["sample"]]
            row["n_events"] = len(events)
            row["n_events_high"] = sum(e["confidence"] == "high" for e in events)

    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.segments.tsv", SEGMENT_COLUMNS, rows_segments)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.events.tsv", EVENT_COLUMNS, rows_events)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.members.tsv", MEMBER_COLUMNS, rows_members)
    high = [e for e in rows_events if e["confidence"] == "high"]
    print(f"{fid}: {len(rows_members)} members, {len(rows_events)} events, {len(high)} high"
          + "".join(f"\n  {e['sample']} {e['chrom']} {e['origin']} {e['composition']} {e['extent']} "
                    f"{fmt(e['length_mb'], 1)} Mb lod {fmt(e['lod'], 1)}" for e in high), file=sys.stderr)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cohort
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_family_tables(directory, label, kind):
    header, rows = None, []
    for path in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, f"*.{label}.{kind}.tsv"))):
        h, r = read_tsv(path)
        header = header or h
        rows += r
    return rows


def cmd_cohort(args):
    members = read_snapshot(args.snapshot)
    expected = {m["fid"] for m in members.values()}
    segments = read_family_tables(args.family_dir, args.label, "segments")
    events = read_family_tables(args.family_dir, args.label, "events")
    tabled = read_family_tables(args.family_dir, args.label, "members")
    found = {r["family_id"] for r in tabled}
    sequenced = {m["fid"] for m in members.values() if m["sequenced"]}
    if found != sequenced:
        absent = sorted(sequenced - found) or sorted(found - expected)
        die("the family tables are not those of the cohort's families: {}".format(", ".join(absent[:20])))

    by_chrom = {}
    for e in events:
        by_chrom.setdefault(e["chrom"], []).append(e)
    for e in events:
        s0, s1 = int(e["start"]), int(e["end"])
        others = set()
        for o in by_chrom[e["chrom"]]:
            if o["family_id"] == e["family_id"]:
                continue
            o0, o1 = int(o["start"]), int(o["end"])
            ov = overlap(s0, s1, o0, o1)
            if ov >= RECURRENT_OVERLAP * (s1 - s0 + 1) and ov >= RECURRENT_OVERLAP * (o1 - o0 + 1):
                others.add(o["family_id"])
        e["recurrent_families"] = len(others)
        e["recurrent"] = "yes" if len(others) >= RECURRENT_MIN_FAMILIES else "no"

    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.segments.tsv", SEGMENT_COLUMNS, segments)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.events.tsv", EVENT_COLUMNS + ["recurrent_families", "recurrent"], events)
    write_tsv(f"{args.out_prefix}.members.tsv", MEMBER_COLUMNS, tabled)
    high = sum(e["confidence"] == "high" and e["recurrent"] == "no" for e in events)
    print(f"{args.cohort}: {len(found)} families, {len(tabled)} members, {len(events)} events, "
          f"{high} high and not recurrent", file=sys.stderr)


def main(argv=None):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command", required=True)

    p = sub.add_parser("family", help="one family's UPD tables, from its BCF query on stdin")
    p.add_argument("--snapshot", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--samples", required=True, help="the BCF's samples, comma-separated, in its order")
    p.add_argument("--coverage-dir")
    p.add_argument("--roh", help="the roh step's roh.tsv of the family")
    p.add_argument("--froh", help="the roh step's froh.tsv of the family")
    p.add_argument("--mask", help="the roh panel's sites, roh/sites.tsv.gz of its bundle: sites outside are dropped")
    p.add_argument("--out-prefix", required=True)
    p.set_defaults(func=cmd_family)

    p = sub.add_parser("cohort", help="the cohort's UPD tables")
    p.add_argument("--cohort", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--snapshot", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--family-dir", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--label", required=True)
    p.add_argument("--out-prefix", required=True)
    p.set_defaults(func=cmd_cohort)

    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if getattr(args, "roh", None) and not getattr(args, "froh", None) or \
            getattr(args, "froh", None) and not getattr(args, "roh", None):
        parser.error("--roh and --froh go together")
    args.func(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
